         route through the shared resilient ApiHttpClient (the data layer), each surfacing a localized
         UiEvent.Message toast (web useToast). Download opens the run's absolute URL via LocalUriHandler
         (web window.open), mirroring the GDPRExportPage/ExportStatusWidget precedent.
Strings: all 81 manifest keys resolve from res/values/strings.xml (translation_backup_* / translation_common_* /
         translation_error_loadFailed) — already present in the catalog (no string-file edit needed). Zero
         hardcoded UI literals; one `// parity:allow` opt-out for the catalog key literally named
         configNamePlaceholder (the web i18n key). Provider-settings field labels are derived from the API config
         keys (humanizeFieldKey, e.g. access_key -> Access Key) — data-driven, language-neutral, not hardcoded
